WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.100
Active contraction keeps adult heart muscle cells from dividing after injury. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 258. After the heart work, an RNA switch that lets a common gut bacterium persist in mucus, a cold virus path that sets off asthma attacks, and a Planetarian spotlight from Qatar. Human cardiac organoids were the test bed in two studies in nature cardiovascular research, on what happens when contraction is briefly switched off.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:31.760
Transient Myosin inhibition with Mavacampton or Afici-Campton

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.700
reactivated the cardiomyosite cell cycle.

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:37.880
Circle mirror remodeling followed that drop in force,

00:00:38.460 --> 00:00:41.420
and metabolic shifts through AKT1 and PDK

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.560
accompanied the remodeling that reopened division programs.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.320
The design paired those human organoids

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:50.320
with direct pharmacological control of contraction force.

00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:53.541
Something most people get wrong about heart muscle

00:00:53.541 --> 00:00:56.701
is the idea that cardiomyosite simply become permanently

00:00:56.701 --> 00:01:02.281
specialized in old, when adult human cardiomyocytes were new at under 1% per year.

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:07.741
That rate is why muscle loss to infarction is rarely replaced by new cardiomyocytes.

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:12.281
The de-differentiated state reverses within hours once contraction resumes.

00:01:13.141 --> 00:01:17.021
Any future regenerative approach will need a temporary window of reduced mechanical

00:01:17.021 --> 00:01:19.921
load without compromising overall cardiac output.

00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:25.865
Helmholtz Institute for RNA-based infection research and JMU Wordsburg scientists.

00:01:25.865 --> 00:01:32.665
In a Fizz.org report, identified a key RNA-based regulator that lets a common gut bacterium handle

00:01:32.665 --> 00:01:35.485
nutrient scarcity inside the intestinal mucus layer.

00:01:36.085 --> 00:01:40.885
The same work ran in collaboration with Vanderbilt Health and also tracks survival under harsh

00:01:40.885 --> 00:01:42.505
conditions in that mucus niche.

00:01:43.085 --> 00:01:47.085
The regulator controls gene expression programs used for nutrient scavenging.

00:01:47.445 --> 00:01:52.405
It also controls programs for stress resistance and for staying put in this specialized layer.

00:01:52.405 --> 00:01:56.865
The findings appear in the current issue of a peer-reviewed microbiology journal.

00:01:57.766 --> 00:02:02.926
Common cold viruses activated distinct signaling route in airway cells that precipitates asthma

00:02:02.926 --> 00:02:06.706
exacerbations, a path mapped in science translational medicine.

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:10.866
The mechanism was dissected in human samples and in model systems.

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:17.640
Charitay and twin-core researchers in a Fizz.org summary found that a virus isolated from West

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.580
African fruit bats bound and entered human cells in laboratory assays.

00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:26.500
diseases. That entry happened despite genetic distance from known respiratory sensitial virus,

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:32.580
or RSV strains. Preexisting human antibodies neutralized the virus in the same experiments.

00:02:33.664 --> 00:02:38.404
University of Hong Kong chemists identified a previously unrecognized cellular structure

00:02:38.664 --> 00:02:43.604
that sequesters certain nucleic acid therapeutics inside compartments away from their intended

00:02:43.604 --> 00:02:50.391
sites of action. The finding was published in Nature Cell Biology. DNA insulators in a science

00:02:50.391 --> 00:02:55.391
Advanced Sciences study from St. Jude, covered by news medical, altered local gene expression

00:02:55.391 --> 00:02:59.071
across 329 mapped lentiviral integration sites.

00:02:59.631 --> 00:03:04.471
The insulators also change chromatin state and three-dimensional genome contacts in ways

00:03:04.471 --> 00:03:06.151
that lower oncogenic potential.

00:03:06.831 --> 00:03:11.031
A machine learning model trained on those features predicted lower risk for insulated

00:03:11.031 --> 00:03:13.471
vectors when applied to patient genomic data.

00:03:14.111 --> 00:03:18.111
No treatment link leukemia has occurred in the XSKYD trial cohort.

00:03:18.111 --> 00:03:18.231
Court.

00:03:19.029 --> 00:03:24.349
Qatar hosts the World Innovation Summit for Health or Wish on November 29th and 30th.

00:03:24.729 --> 00:03:27.829
Times Kuwait notes, under the theme, The New Health Span.

00:03:28.549 --> 00:03:33.589
Flagship reports will cover longevity science, artificial intelligence integration, fertility

00:03:33.589 --> 00:03:35.069
and healthcare financing.

00:03:35.669 --> 00:03:40.769
Discussions will examine how advances in cellular biology and epigenetics can extend the

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:41.929
period of healthy life.

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:46.009
Those sessions also take up equitable access and ethical questions.

00:03:46.009 --> 00:03:50.509
Dr. David Sinclair is scheduled to deliver a keynote on aging biology.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:55.149
The meeting's stated aim is narrowing the gap between lifespan and health span.

00:03:56.145 --> 00:04:01.285
Southern China produced fossil teeth from two caves in a nature paper noted by Fizz.org.

00:04:01.805 --> 00:04:03.885
One set shows Denisovan affinities.

00:04:04.365 --> 00:04:08.565
A second, more primitive lineage, has an exact placement that remains unresolved.

00:04:09.105 --> 00:04:12.045
The four specimens date to the middle and late Pleistocene.

00:04:12.045 --> 00:04:18.023
The smart Jan prototype from the University of Dusto combines near-infrared spectroscopy

00:04:18.023 --> 00:04:22.383
with machine learning algorithms to identify lipid transfer protein allergens.

00:04:22.903 --> 00:04:27.423
Those allergens include ProP3 in Peach and AraH9 in Peanut.

00:04:27.903 --> 00:04:30.723
The system produces a spectral fingerprint in seconds.

00:04:31.303 --> 00:04:34.583
Earlier tests also showed detection of gluten and meat bacteria.

00:04:35.223 --> 00:04:37.843
The study is published in Food Analytical Methods.

00:04:37.843 --> 00:04:43.261
Engineers developed an implantable device that harvests ultrasound energy for operation.

00:04:43.741 --> 00:04:47.021
It emits an optical signal to indicate its structural integrity.

00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:51.981
The approach removes the need for batteries and allows external inspection of device condition

00:04:51.981 --> 00:04:53.301
after implantation.

00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:59.557
Job satisfaction in small and medium-sized enterprises, in the International Journal of Economics

00:04:59.557 --> 00:05:04.977
and Business Research, showed a stronger statistical association with perceived work-life balance

00:05:04.977 --> 00:05:06.217
than with salary level.

00:05:06.217 --> 00:05:11.117
Flexible working arrangements were also weaker predictors than that balance measure.

00:05:11.871 --> 00:05:16.511
Along the Pacific coast, researchers used drones to locate southern resident orcas.

00:05:17.131 --> 00:05:22.171
A trained detection dog locates floating fecal samples for hormone and contaminant analysis.

00:05:22.811 --> 00:05:27.211
The method has been applied each fall in recent years and avoids direct animal handling.

00:05:28.131 --> 00:05:33.351
A team at the University of Hong Kong and Tsinghua University quantified the maximum elastic

00:05:33.351 --> 00:05:38.891
deformation between layers in graphite and hexagonal boron nitride before irreversible

00:05:38.891 --> 00:05:39.771
sliding occurs.

00:05:40.391 --> 00:05:42.591
The measurements appear in nature communications.

00:05:43.625 --> 00:05:48.805
Briefly, three Israeli researchers, writing in the Jerusalem Post, described the cognitive

00:05:48.805 --> 00:05:51.785
steps that produce sudden insight during problem-solving.

00:05:52.225 --> 00:05:57.505
Before we go, larger animal tests are now asking whether that kind of temporary load window

00:05:57.505 --> 00:05:59.625
on heart muscle can be engineered safely.

